signatures.summary:
Reconstruct a single mobject from a serialized node, or `null` when the type
is unknown (unregistered or marked `unknown`). Known children are attached;
unknown children are dropped.

examples:
```typescript
// Create a die face showing 5
const face = new DiceFace({ value: 5 });

// Create a smaller red die face showing 3
const redDie = new DiceFace({
  value: 3,
  size: 1,
  backgroundColor: '#CC0000',
  dotColor: WHITE,
});

// Show all six faces in a row
const dice = new VGroup();
for (let i = 1; i <= 6; i++) {
  dice.add(new DiceFace({ value: i }));
}
dice.arrange(RIGHT, 0.3);
```

